  declared  bsnwin                 \BsNWinA = 38; \BsNWinB = 374
            reason: the same channelisation split over the BRIGHT STARS THE SAMPLE EXCLUDES -- the holding that would be admitted if the Gaia DR3 parallax requirement were dropped -- and not a second count of the searched windows: 38 fine and 374 coarse, in neither \NWinA nor \NWinB
  declared  fracmax                \HoFracMax = 0.47; \RcFracMax = 0.997
            reason: the largest fraction of the discovery amplitude the repeat coverage still excludes, in the reserved hold-out search against the primary census.  Two populations, and the difference is the point: every hold-out crossing is excluded at 0.47 of its amplitude or less, while in the census the individual limits run all the way to 1.00, which is why the census median is reported as a median and never as a bound on the set
  declared  fracmed                \RcFracMed = 0.43; \RfiFracMed = 0.5
            reason: TWO DIFFERENT FRACTIONS OF TWO DIFFERENT THINGS, and only the word "frac" is shared.  RcFracMed is the median fraction of the DISCOVERY AMPLITUDE that the repeat coverage excludes, over the crossings that carry an exclusion.  RfiFracMed is the median fractional POSITION of a released peak inside its own spectral window, which is the fixed-intermediate-frequency test of the interference appendix and is 0.50 because the positions are uniform.  Neither is a bound and they are not the same quantity in any sense
  declared  ncross                 \HoNCross = 8; \LdgNCrossB = 4
            reason: TWO POPULATIONS, NOT TWO COUNTS OF ONE.  \HoNCross is every crossing found in the hold-out, i.e. in the execution blocks the identifier rule of App. B.1 reserves, of either class (8 events, which is the set the transfer ratio R2-4 asks about is measured on).  \LdgNCrossB is the Class B crossings of the PRIMARY CENSUS (4), all of them in the one execution block that fails the data-quality criterion, which is the fact R1-3 requires the principal result to state.  The hold-out and the census share no execution block at all (holdout_v412 H4), so neither count is any part of the other
  declared  ninetymult             \EirpNinetyMultA = 3.03; \EirpNinetyMultB = 4.17
            reason: the completeness multiplier measured separately per class, which is the whole point of measuring it per class
  declared  nstar                  \DqNStar = 2; \HoNStar = 36; \SfNStar = 90
            reason: the stars of the windows the data-quality rule flags; the reserved hold-out's stars; and the searched sample -- three sets, three counts
  declared  ntested                \HoNTested = 7; \RcNTested = 38; \VerNTested = 1657
            reason: unattributed crossings tested for recurrence against windows matched to an ACA geometry-verification record -- different things counted, as queue entry 31 sets out
  declared  nwin                   \DqNWin = 5; \HoNWin = 315; \PbNWin = 1663
            reason: windows flagged by the data-quality rule; the reserved hold-out's windows; and the windows of the primary-beam audit, which is the whole release -- three sets, three counts.  'ScrNWinA' and 'PxaNWin' left this group when Ruling 1 removed the screen cost from the paper and the parallax row from the budget
  declared  sbpriornstar           \SbPriorNStarA = 40; \SbPriorNStarB = 17
            reason: the star counts of the TWO PUBLISHED SEARCHES above 30 GHz, not of two classes of this one: Steffes & DeBoer's 40 solar-type stars within 23 pc and Mauersberger et al.'s 17 Vega-like and solar-type targets.  The A/B suffix here distinguishes two other people's papers, which is the one case where the class heuristic means something else
  declared  scimunratio            \ScImUnRatioA = 1.37; \ScImUnRatioB = 0.93
            reason: the measured parent-to-crossing amplitude ratio at each of the two crossings, each read in the block that observed its own parent frequency: two independent measurements, and the point of both is that each falls short of the leakage a 10 dB image rejection would need
  declared  stars                  \HoStars = 36; \NStars = 90
